                                "sense_id": "806510b1-9aaa-39af-b1ba-d88576e27555",
                                "text": "He tied the apron on with a little bow behind and strode to the big marble slab like a towelled man to a Turkish bath."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ff7ca87-b91b-404e-8d96-b7f43de52d7e",
                                "sense_id": "806510b1-9aaa-39af-b1ba-d88576e27555",
                                "text": "Thick atmospheres obscure the fuzzy figures surrounding, towelled men wearing flip-flops, smearing shaving gel across their chins, sighing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "efd5301f-8f73-4fdf-8b5d-54f7dc34f2c7",
                                "sense_id": "806510b1-9aaa-39af-b1ba-d88576e27555",
                                "text": "At the other end of the spectrum, Gunjal’s ‘Someday’ traces the movements of a modern young woman (signs of ‘modernity’ include cigarette smoking) from the shower (followed by a panel of two towelled women) to the streets where she is subjected to sexual harassment."
                            }
